# {{NAME}}

An external oveRTOS application.

## Build

```bash
make host.posix.{{CONFIG_NAME}}     # POSIX host
make qemu.freertos.{{CONFIG_NAME}}  # QEMU + FreeRTOS

make            # download, configure, build
make run        # launch (POSIX) or boot in QEMU
make flash      # program hardware (if board target supports it)
```

`OVE_DIR` is set in `Makefile`. Override per invocation:

```bash
make OVE_DIR=/other/path/to/oveRTOS host.posix.{{CONFIG_NAME}} && make
```

## Layout

```
{{NAME}}/
├── Makefile       # 3-line entry; includes $(OVE_DIR)/config/make/ove_app.mk
├── app.yaml       # manifest (language, sources, required CONFIG_OVE_*)
├── include/
│   └── app_conf.h # app-local tunables
├── src/
│   └── app.c      # ove_main() entry point
└── output/        # generated workspace (gitignored)
```

## Adding modules

Edit `app.yaml`'s `defconfig:` list. Common additions:

```yaml
defconfig:
  - CONFIG_OVE_QUEUE=y      # message queues
  - CONFIG_OVE_TIMER=y      # software timers
  - CONFIG_OVE_NET=y        # sockets / TCP / UDP
  - CONFIG_OVE_LVGL=y       # LVGL display
  - CONFIG_OVE_NVS=y        # non-volatile storage
```

